[ti:Week05-Wed.mp3]

[00:00.00]cite 熟义 v. 引证；引用；传唤；嘉奖 示例 ① The third rule is to be ready to cite options and consequences. 第三条规则是，时刻准备着列举出备选方案，并指出相应后果。（2011. 6）② She cited her heavy workload as the reason for her breakdown. 她说繁重的工作负荷是导致她累垮的原因。
[00:05.28]contaminate 熟义 v. 污染，弄脏；玷污 示例 ① We know that it produces toxic (and radioactive) wastewater that contaminates drinking water; there is reason to suspect, despite industry denials, that it also contaminates groundwater; and the heavy trucking required for fracking inflicts major damage on roads. 我们知道它产生对饮用水有污染的有毒（还具有放射性）的废水；尽管该行业予以否认，我们有理由怀疑，这项技术同时也污染地下水，还有，提供液压破碎法所需要的重型卡车运输也给道路带来严重的破坏。（The New York Times）② We shouldn't eat the contaminated foods. 我们不应该吃受到污染的食物。
[00:17.29]numerous 熟义 a. 众多的，许多的 示例 ① In time, Italians, Romanians and members of other so-called inferior races became exemplary Americans and contributed greatly, in ways too numerous to detail, to the building of this magnificent nation. 一段时间之后，意大利人、罗马尼亚人以及其他被称作“劣等民族” 的人最后成了美国人中的典范之士，以各种各样的方式为建设这个伟大的国家而贡献良多。（2008. 12）② She has been late on numerous occasions. 她已经迟到无数次了。
[00:26.60]soar 熟义 v. 急升，猛增；升空，升腾；高飞，翱翔 示例 ① Imports, which soared to $200.3 billion in the month, are subtracted in the calculation of gross domestic product. 这个月的进口额猛增至2003亿美元，但在计算国内生产总值时是被减去的。（2011. 12）② Unemployment has soared to 17%. 失业率猛升到了17%。
[00:32.67]directly 熟义 ad. 直接地；正好地；立即；很快 示例 ① David Card, an economist at UC Berkeley, notes that the ones who profit most directly from immigrants' low-cost labor are businesses and employers— meatpacking plants in Nebraska, for instance, or agricultural businesses in California. 加州大学伯克利分校的经济学家戴维•卡德指出，从低廉移民劳动力身上直接获益的是企业和雇主，比如说内布拉斯加州的肉类包装工厂或者加州的农业企业。（2011. 6）② This pesticide is diluted with water and applied directly to the fields. 这种杀虫剂被用水稀释后直接施用在田地里。
[00:44.09]detective 熟义 n. 侦探，警探；私人侦探 示例 ① Yes, you must, really, if you're writing the classical detective story, because it must be so carefully plotted and so carefully clued. 是的，事实上，如果你正在写传统的侦探小说，就必须如此（即知道后面要怎么写），因为侦探小说的情节必须设计巧妙，线索必须安排得当。（2010. 12）② She unbent her mind by reading detective stories. 她通过读侦探小说来放松心情。
[00:51.94]despite 熟义 prep. 即使，尽管 示例 ① Despite diminishing—and eventually disappearing—summer Arctic ice, polar bears will not become extinct. 尽管夏季北极冰川正在融减并将最终消失， 但北极熊不会灭绝。（2013. 6）② Despite the fact that he made all his efforts to control it, his voice was shaking. 尽管他竭尽全力控制自己，但他的声音仍然在颤抖。
[00:59.01]craft 熟义 n. 手艺；技巧‖v. （尤指用手工）精心制作 示例 ① Meanwhile, New Orleans officials have crafted a plan to use buses and trains to evacuate the sick and the disabled. 同时，新奥尔良的官员们已经拟定了一个使用公共汽车和火车疏散病人和残疾人的计划。（2007. 6）② She knew how to win by craft and diplomacy what she could not gain by force. 她知道如何通过计谋和外交手腕赢得她用武力无法得到的东西。
[01:06.72]intricate 熟义 a. 错综复杂的 示例 ① You develop in-depth knowledge of the intricate structure of the language. 你（会）深入了解关于语言复杂结构方面的知识。（2009. 6）② The intricate machine requires a skilled operator. 这种复杂的机器需由技能熟练的人操作。
[01:11.91]reliance 熟义 n. 依赖，依靠；信任，信心 示例 ① Ongoing soreness in Bryant's knee and ankle coupled with the team's heavy reliance in him played a role in the Lakers' championship run coming to an end in 2011. 科比膝盖和脚踝的持续疼痛，以及球队对他的严重依赖，导致湖人队的三连冠梦想在2011年宣告结束。（The Los Angeles Times）② He wouldn't place too much reliance on these figures. 他不会太相信这些数字的。
[01:20.21]apply 熟义 v. 申请；使用；涉及 示例 ① Examine the skills and knowledge that you have and identify how they can apply to your desired occupation. 检查你所拥有的技能和知识，看它们如何能应用到你渴望的职位上。（2007. 6）② I should apply the job in person by letter. 我应该亲自写信申请那份工作。
[01:25.96]estimate 熟义 n.（对数量、成本等的）估计，估价；报价；判断 v. 估价；估算 示例 ① In fact, by some estimates, the value of parental investments in children, investments of time and money (including lost wages), is equal to 20-30% of gross domestic product. 事实上，根据某些估测， 父母在孩子身上投入的价值——时间和金钱方面的投入（包括由于照顾孩子而损失的工资），相当于国民生产总值的20%至 30%。（2010. 6）② He can give you a rough estimate of the amount of wood you will need. 他可以帮你粗略地估计一下你所需要的木材量。
[01:36.03]remark 熟义 n. 谈论；引人注目‖v. 说起，谈论；评论 示例 ① He also famously remarked that all of man's problems come from his inability to sit quietly in a room alone. 他曾有句名言：人们所有的问题都源于不能在房间里独自静坐下来。（2012. 12）② The editor remarked that article was well written. 编者评论说那篇文章写得很好。
[01:42.37]tropical 熟义 a. 热带的，来自热带的 示例 ① On July 19, 1979, there was a very strong tropical storm in the Caribbean Sea near the Venezuelan coast very close to Tobago. 1979年7月19日，一次非常强烈的热带风暴席卷了委内瑞拉海岸周边距多巴哥很近的加勒比海域。（www.toptenz.net） ② This is a tropical island. 这是一个热带岛屿。
[01:48.85]consistent 熟义 a. 一致的；连续的；符合的；相互连贯的 示例 ① A simple and consistent set of endings indicates grammatical functions of words. 简单且一致的结尾表明了单词的语法功能。② The results are not entirely consistent with our early research. 这些结果与我们早些时候的研究不完全相符。
[01:54.63]statue 熟义 n. 雕塑，雕像 示例 ① New York's iconic Statue of Liberty reopened to the public, eight months after Superstorm Sandy damaged its island. 纽约标志性的自由女神像在超级风暴桑迪损坏自由岛八个月后向公众开放。（The Washington Post）② There is a statue of Nelson in Trafalgar Square. 在特拉法加广场有一尊纳尔逊的塑像。
[02:01.23]reference 熟义 n. 提及；参考；推荐信 示例 ① Here, the important aspect is to compare with an appropriate reference group. 此时，重要的方面是与合适的参考群体相比较。（2012. 12）② He made no reference to his illness but only to his future plans. 他没有提到他的病，只说了他未来的规划。
[02:06.89]impulse 熟义 n. 冲动；脉冲；刺激 示例 ① The human brain may contain up to one trillion neurons. These nerve cells are interconnected, so that they can transmit electrical impulses—and information—to other cells. 人类的大脑可能包含着多达1万亿的神经细胞。这些神经细胞是相互关联的，因此它们可以传递电脉冲和信息到其他的细胞。（National Geographic）② He resisted the impulse to laugh. 他强忍着没有笑出来。
[02:15.16]evaporate 熟义 v. （使）蒸发；（逐渐）消失 示例 ① We just make some half-hearted resolution and it evaporates after a week or two. 我们仅仅下了一些半心半意的决心， 而这些决心会在一两周后消失殆尽。（2007. 6） ② His confidence has now completely evaporated. 他的信心已经完全消失了。
[02:20.65]boundary 熟义 n. 边界，界限 示例 ① The drive way or the fence between you is not really a cold shoulder but a clear boundary. 你们（邻里）之间的车道或围栏并非真的意味着冷淡，而是清晰的界限。（2008. 6）② The fence marks the boundary between his property and hers. 那道篱笆是他和她住宅之间的分界。
[02:26.49]precaution 熟义 n. 预防措施，预防 示例 ① A few precautions can help most climbers avoid altitude sickness. 一些预防措施可以帮助大多数爬山者避免高原反应。（2012. 12）② You must keep the letter as a precaution. 你必须保存好这封信，以防万一。
[02:31.22]convert 熟义 v. (使)转变，转化；（使） 皈依 n. 改变宗教（或信仰、观点）的人 示例 ① Dakota Gasification of North Dakota captures CO2 at a plant that converts coal into synthetic natural gas. 北达科他州的达科他气化公司在一家将煤转化成合成天然气的工厂收集二氧化碳气体。（2012. 6）② He was soon converted to the socialist cause. 他不久便转而献身于社会主义事业了。
[02:38.11]toxic 熟义 a. 有毒的，引起中毒的 示例 ① Ideally, such a source would be safe in that it could not be made into weapons and would not make hazardous or toxic waste or carbon dioxide, the main greenhouse gas blamed for global warming. 理论上，这样一种能源之所以安全，是因为它不能用来制成武器，也不会生成危险的或有毒的废物或二氧化碳这一对全球变暖负有责任的主要的温室气体。（2008. 6）② Many pesticides are toxic. 许多杀虫剂都是有毒的。
[02:46.57]condense 熟义 v.（由气体）冷凝；（使）浓缩，（使）变浓；压缩（文字、信息等） 示例 ① Air was first liquefied in 1883, using essentially the same process as today—ie, compressing it to 200 atmospheres, cooling it to -190℃, and then letting it suddenly expand and condense. 1883年，人类首次液化空气，工艺流程与今天的类似，比如说，以200个大气压将其压缩，冷却至零下190摄氏度后，令其急速释放和浓缩。（The Economist） ② You can condense the soup by boiling it for several minutes. 你可以煮几分钟把汤熬浓。
[02:56.65]fertiliser 熟义 n. 肥料 示例 ① In this method of farming, seeds and fertiliser are put into the soil through small cuts made in the surface of the ground. 使用这种方法耕作，种子和肥料可以通过对地表的小程度破坏投入土壤。（2006. 12）② This factory turns out chemical fertiliser. 这家工厂生产化肥。
[03:02.75]stationary 熟义 a. 不动的，静止的；不变的，稳定的 示例 ① For example, an inability to perceive movement even though the individual can see stationary objects results from damage to part of the temporal lobe, and an inability to recognise faces is caused by damage to the fusiform gyrus. 例如，一个人即使可以看见静止的物体，也不能感知运动，是由于他的部分脑颞叶受到了损伤；而不能识别人的面相，则是因为纺锤形脑回受到了损伤。（The Economist） ② A stationary object is easy to be aimed at. 一个静止不动的物体是容易瞄准的。
[03:13.17]licence 熟义 n. 许可证，执照 示例 ① It can include them in subscription deals sold to libraries or sell them individually under a consumer licence. 它 （谷歌）可以将这些图书包括在出售给图书馆的订阅协议中，也可以按照消费许可单独出售。（2011. 12）② His licence was suspended for drunk driving. 他的驾驶执照因酒后开车被暂时吊销。
[03:19.63]loyalty 熟义 n. 忠诚，忠实 示例 ① Firms invest a lot on the image of their brands to foster sales and loyalty. 各公司在品牌上投入了很多，以促进销售和增强忠诚度。② He swore his loyalty to the king. 他宣誓效忠国王。
[03:23.77]artificial 熟义 a. 人工的；人造的；假的；做作的，虚假的 示例 ① Some law firms now use artificial intelligence software to scan and read mountains of legal documents, work that previously was performed by highly-paid human lawyers. 一些律师事务所现在使用人工智能软件扫描和阅读大量的法律文件，这些工作之前都是由领着高薪的人工律师来完成的。（2012. 12）② Her artificial gaiety disguised an inner sadness. 她用虚假的快乐掩饰内心的悲痛。
[03:32.50]embody 熟义 v. 具体表现，体现；包括，包含 示例 ① We honor them not only because they are guardians of our liberty, but because they embody the spirit of service: a willingness to find meaning in something greater than themselves. 我们尊敬他们，不仅因为他们捍卫了我们的自由，更因为他们代表着服务的精神，他们自愿追寻比自身的价值更伟大的意义。（The New York Times）② She embodied the idea in her painting. 她把那个概念具体地表现在她的绘画中。
[03:41.26]kin 熟义 n. [pl.](统称)家属，亲戚 示例 ① Like its modern-day kin, it appears to have moved mostly by leaping between twigs, which it grasped with all four limbs. 与其现代同族一样，在小树枝之间跳跃似乎是它（眼镜猴）最主要的运动方式，跳跃时它用四肢抓住枝条。（The Economist）② Please be far away from tobaccos for you and your kin's healthy! 为了您和家人的健康，请远离香烟！
[03:48.71]parameter 熟义 n. 决定因素；范围，界限；参量，参数；特点 示例 ① An expert associated with the site evaluates whether the price, the parameters, and the schedule are reasonable; if not, Navalny trumpets the alleged fraud on his blog, often causing the agency responsible to be buried in hostile correspondence. 网站还会请来专家对价格、参数和工程进度进行评估，以确定是否合理；如果不合理的话，纳瓦尔尼会在他的个人博客上进行公开，一旦予以公开， 涉事部门通常会被群众的敌对信件淹没。（The New Yorker）② He had to work within the parameters that had already been established. 他必须在已设定的范围内工作。
[04:00.82]moisture 熟义 n. 潮湿，湿气；水，水分 示例 ① A workman daubed gray putty around the edges of the wall to prevent moisture from seeping in. 一个工匠在墙壁的边缘涂抹灰浆，防止湿气潜入屋内。（The Washington Post）② The hot sun draws up the moisture from the earth. 炎热的太阳蒸发了土壤中的湿气。
[04:06.69]item 熟义 n. 条款，项目；一件商品（或物品）； 一则或一条新闻 示例 ① The left side of most vertebrate brains seems to process and control feeding, for example. Since the left hemisphere processes input from the right side of the body, that means animals as diverse as fish, toads and birds are more likely to attack prey or food items if they view them with their right eye. 例如，大部分脊椎动物大脑的左半球似乎是处理和控制进食的。因为左半球处理来自身体右侧信息的输入，这就意味着不同种类的动物，如鱼、蟾蜍、鸟，如果它们用右眼看到猎物或食物，则更可能捕食猎物或进食。（New Scientist）② The computer was his largest single item of expenditure. 电脑是他花钱最多的单品。
[04:19.98]extensive 熟义 a. 广阔的，广大的；大量的；广泛的， 广博的 示例 ① The media, including this newspaper, are giving the subject extensive coverage. 包括本报在内的媒体都在对这个话题进行广泛的报道。（2010. 12） ② He suffered extensive injuries in the accident. 他在事故中受了重伤。
[04:25.50]strain 熟义 n. 压力；劳损‖v. 损伤；尽力；过度使用；拉紧 示例 ① Others highlight the strain that undocumented immigrants place on public services, like schools, hospitals, and jails. 其他人强调，没有身份的移民给公共服务设施如学校、医院和监狱方面带来压力。（2011. 6）② He strained his ears to catch what they were saying. 他竖起耳朵去听他们在说什么。
[04:32.47]approve 熟义 v. 赞成；批准；认可 示例 ① Probably the most incredible aspect of this proposed space tour was that NASA approved of it. 或许这次被提议的太空之旅最令人难以置信的方面是美国宇航局同意了。（2006. 12）② I presume you will approve of the plan. 我相信你会赞成这个计划。
[04:37.91]elegant 熟义 a. 优雅的；漂亮雅致的；简练的 示例 ① The French have always loved Apple. Its elegant products and nimble operating systems, and its underdog struggles against IBM and Microsoft in the 1980s, are especially appealing in a country that prides itself on being chic, clever and revolutionary. 法国人一向对苹果情有独钟。其精致雅观的外形，灵活的操作系统，以及20世纪80年代在与IBM和微软较量中的力争上游，无不令法国这个崇尚时尚、机智和革命的国家为之动容，被其吸引。（The Economist）② This room has an elegant atmosphere with these furniture. 这些家具使这个房间具有一种优雅的气氛。
[04:49.88]speculate 熟义 v. 推测，猜测；投机，做投机买卖 示例 ① A set of accompanying papers describe the fossils and speculate about their significance. 一组随附的论文对这些化石进行了描述并对其意义做出了推测。（The Economist）② We all speculate about the reason for his resignation. 我们所有人都推测他辞职的原因。
[04:56.04]faithful 熟义 a. 忠实的；忠诚的；如实的；可信任的 示例 ① At these moments, America has carried on not simply because of the skill or vision of those in high office, but because We the People have remained faithful to the ideals of our forbearers, and true to our founding documents. 在这些时刻，支持美国前进的不仅仅是领导人的能力和远见，也在于美国人民对国家先驱者理想的信仰，以及对美国建国文献的忠诚。（The New York Times）② He was rewarded for his 30 years' faithful service with the company. 他为公司忠诚服务了30 年，因而获得奖励。
